   "*": "==Box office collection==\nThe [[List of highest-grossing Kannada films|highest-grossing Kannada films]] released in 2025, by worldwide [[box office]] [[gross revenue]], are as follows.The total collection of sandalwood movies in 2025 is 1,500 crores. The rank of the films in the following table depends on the estimate of worldwide collections as reported by organizations classified as green by Wikipedia.{{efn|See [[WP:RSP]], [[WP:ICTFSOURCES]]}} There is no official tracking of [[List of highest-grossing films in India|domestic box office figures]] within India.\n<!-- Note: When contributing to this section, please ensure that all references used for ranking are from green sources as specified in [[WP:ICTFSOURCES]] or [[WP:RSPSS]]. It is crucial to verify that the references do not originate from unreliable sources, in accordance with [[WP:FRUIT]]. Use '!scope=\"row\" style with background:#b6fcb6;' to indicate running films when applicable.-->\n:{{legend|#b6fcb6|size=50%|''Background shading indicates that a film is currently showing in theatres worldwide.''}}\n{| class=\"wikitable\"\n|-\n| style=\"text-align:center; background:#ccc;\"|'''#'''\n|Implies that the film is multilingual and the gross collection figure includes the worldwide collection of the other simultaneously filmed version.\n|}\n{| class=\"wikitable sortable\" style=\" margin:auto;\"\n|+Highest worldwide gross of 2025\n|-\n! Rank \n! Title\n! Production company \n! Worldwide gross\n!Ref\n|-\n!1\n|''[[Kantara: Chapter 1]] ''\n|[[Hombale Films]]\n| style=\"text-align:right; \" | {{INR|850–852 crore}}\n| style=\"text-align: center;\" | {{efn|''Kantara: Chapter 1''{{'}}s reported worldwide grosses vary between ₹850 crore (''[[Deccan Chronicle]]''<ref>{{cite web |title=‘Kantara’ Goes Global in English |url=https://www.deccanchronicle.com/tabloid/hyderabad-chronicle/kantara-goes-global-in-english-1911794 |website=Deccan Chronicle |access-date=17 June 2026 |date=22 October 2025}}</ref>, ''[[Cinema Express]]''<ref>{{cite web |title=Rishab Shetty marks a unique milestone in Indian cinema with Kantara films |url=https://www.cinemaexpress.com/kannada/news/2026/Jan/02/rishab-shetty-marks-a-unique-milestone-in-indian-cinema-with-kantara-films |website=Cinema Express |access-date=17 June 2026 |date=2 January 2026}}</ref>, ''[[The New Indian Express]]''<ref>{{cite web |title=Kantara: Chapter 1 earns Oscar eligibility, puts Kannada cinema on the global map |url=https://www.newindianexpress.com/entertainment/kannada/2026/Jan/10/kannadanews2026jan10kantara-chapter-1-earns-oscar-eligibility-puts-kannada-cinema-on-the-global-map |website=The New Indian Express |access-date=17 June 2026 |date=10 January 2026}}</ref>, and ''[[DNA India]]''<ref>{{cite web |title=Kantara Chapter 1: Rishab Shetty's epic crosses Rs 600 crore in India, beats Chhaava to become highest-grossing film in India in 2025 |url=https://www.dnaindia.com/entertainment/report-kantara-chapter-1-rishab-shetty-epic-crosses-rs-600-crore-in-india-beats-chhaava-to-become-highest-grossing-film-in-india-in-2025-3186064 |website=DNA India |access-date=17 June 2026 |date=31 October 2025}}</ref>) – ₹852 crore (''[[Deccan Herald]]''<ref>{{cite web |title=Rishab Shetty's 'Kantara: Chapter 1' crosses Rs 852 crore at box-office, sets new record |url=https://www.deccanherald.com/entertainment/rishab-shettys-kantara-chapter-1-crosses-rs-852-crore-at-box-office-sets-new-record-3777835 |website=Deccan Herald |access-date=17 June 2026 |date=28 October 2025}}</ref> and ''[[News18]]''<ref>{{cite web |title=Did Rishab Shetty Make Kantara Chapter 1 For Money? Director Reveals 'I Knew I Had To...' |url=https://www.news18.com/movies/south-cinema/did-rishab-shetty-make-kantara-chapter-1-for-money-director-reveals-i-knew-i-had-to-ws-kl-9671788.html |website=News18 |access-date=17 June 2026}}</ref>)}}\n|-\n! style=\"text-align: center;\" |2\n| ''[[Mahavatar Narsimha]]''{{efn-lg|name=\"mn\"|There is no clear evidence of a primary lan